---
import PublicLayout from '../../../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
import GuidePdfPreview from '../../../components/guides/GuidePdfPreview.astro';
import GuidePageGallery from '../../../components/guides/GuidePageGallery.astro';
import {cycle,examples,handover,familyTalk,issues,prompt} from '../../../../scripts/lib/responsibility-guide-content.mjs';
const pdf='/downloads/family-responsibility-system.pdf';
const images=[1,2,3,4].map(n=>`/images/guides/responsibility-guide-page-${n}.webp`);
const art=(name:string)=>`/assets/icons/ofc/guides/responsibility/${name}.png`;
---
<PublicLayout title="The Family Responsibility System: Help Kids Own Jobs Without Nagging" description="Stop managing every household job. A free family responsibility system with six-step handover, family ownership meeting, troubleshooting and illustrated four-page PDF." width="full" ogType="article">
<div class="omc-guide text-[#545454]">
<section class="px-5 py-9 sm:px-8 sm:py-14"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm font-medium"><a href="/guides" class="underline underline-offset-4">Guides</a><span aria-hidden="true" class="mx-2">/</span>The Family Responsibility System</nav>
<header class="mx-auto mt-9 max-w-[52rem] text-center">
<p class="eyebrow">SHARED RESPONSIBILITY · LESS MENTAL LOAD</p>
<h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-[clamp(2.4rem,6vw,4.25rem)] leading-[1.09] tracking-tight">Stop being the only person who notices what needs doing.</h1>
<p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-[42rem] text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.8] sm:text-lg">Everyone says they'll help. But if you're still assigning, reminding and checking every job, you're carrying the responsibility. Here's how to hand over the whole job so everyone can contribute.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-xs text-[#777]">Free practical guide · Four-page illustrated printable · Based on our family ownership framework</p>
</header>
<div class="mt-10 grid items-center gap-8 border-t-[5px] border-[#CDDDE1] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6 sm:p-10 md:grid-cols-[1.15fr_.85fr]">
<div><p class="eyebrow">FREE PRINTABLE · FOUR US LETTER PAGES</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl leading-tight">The Family Responsibility System</h2>
<p class="mt-4 max-w-lg text-sm leading-[1.8] sm:text-base">Understand helping versus owning, teach one whole job, agree on family responsibilities and solve the problems that make everything fall back on Mom.</p>
<ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed"><li>✓ Four parts of owning a whole job</li><li>✓ Six-step handover and one-job agreement</li><li>✓ A family ownership worksheet and real-life fixes</li></ul>
<a href={pdf} download="OMC-Family-Responsibility-System.pdf" class="btn-primary mt-7">Download the free PDF</a>
<p class="mt-2 text-xs text-[#6f6a65]">Four pages · Email requested on first download · Marketing optional</p></div>
<div class="py-5"><GuidePdfPreview pdf={pdf} images={images} title="The Family Responsibility System"/></div></div>
<nav aria-label="On this page" class="mt-8 border-t border-[#ded8d2] pt-5"><p class="label mb-3 text-[#6f6a65]">IN THIS GUIDE</p><div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 sm:flex sm:flex-wrap sm:gap-3"><a class="guide-anchor" href="#ownership">Helping vs. owning</a><a class="guide-anchor" href="#handover">Hand over a job</a><a class="guide-anchor" href="#meeting">Our family team</a><a class="guide-anchor" href="#problems">Troubleshooting</a><a class="guide-anchor max-sm:col-span-2" href="#printable">Free printable</a></div></nav>
</div></section>

<section id="ownership" class="px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">01 · MORE THAN HELPING</p><h2 class="section-heading">Helping waits to be asked. Ownership carries the whole job.</h2>
<p class="section-lede">You can share the hands-on work without sharing the mental load. Real ownership means knowing when a job needs doing, starting without someone managing it, finishing and checking the result. Children learn this gradually, with age-appropriate support.</p>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">{cycle.map(([icon,title,detail],i)=><article class="border-t-[5px] border-[#CDDDE1] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-5"><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src={art(icon)} width="64" height="64" loading="lazy" alt="" class:list={['object-contain',icon==='eye'?'size-12':'size-16']}/><span class="font-serif text-2xl text-[#6f6a65]">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span></div><h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-xl">{title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}</div>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">{examples.map(([icon,title,detail])=><article class="border border-[#e4dcd3] p-5"><img src={art(icon)} width="60" height="60" loading="lazy" alt="" class="size-[60px] object-contain"/><h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-xl">{title}</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}</div>
<p class="mt-7 text-sm leading-[1.8]">On page one of the PDF, list three jobs you're still managing. Choose only one to hand over first. Real independence comes through practice, not a sudden announcement.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="handover" class="bg-[#D4DFC4]/20 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">02 · TEACH IT THEN HAND IT OVER</p><h2 class="section-heading">Six steps for giving someone a whole responsibility.</h2><p class="section-lede">This matches the ownership teaching process in November's <em>Our Family, Our Team</em> Club resource. Don't assume a child already knows what a complete job involves. Show it, practice it and give the remembering a new home.</p>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">{handover.map(([icon,title,detail],i)=><article class="border-t-[5px] border-[#D4DFC4] bg-white p-6"><div class="flex items-center gap-4"><img src={art(icon)} width="64" height="64" loading="lazy" alt="" class="size-16 object-contain"/><span class="font-serif text-2xl text-[#6f6a65]">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span></div><h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-xl">{title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}</div>
<div class="mt-8 border-l-4 border-[#D4DFC4] bg-white p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">Make one real handover agreement.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Page two gives you five lines: <strong>Job, Owner, When It Starts, Finished Means, Help or Supplies Needed.</strong> That turns a vague request into a responsibility someone can actually practice.</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Example: “After dinner, I clear my place. I'm finished when my dishes are in the agreed spot and crumbs are wiped.”</p></div>
</div></section>

<section id="meeting" class="px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">03 · OUR FAMILY, OUR TEAM</p><h2 class="section-heading">Everyone has a part. Including grown-ups.</h2><p class="section-lede">Use a short family conversation to agree on one real responsibility per person. A three-year-old needs help; an older child can carry more. Grown-ups own the jobs that need grown-ups, especially safety and scheduling.</p>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">{familyTalk.map(([icon,title,detail])=><article class="border-t-[5px] border-[#F1D8A8] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><div class="flex items-center gap-4"><img src={art(icon)} width="58" height="58" loading="lazy" alt="" class="size-[58px] object-contain"/><h3 class="font-serif text-xl">{title}</h3></div><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}</div>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-6 bg-[#CDDDE1]/35 p-7 sm:p-9 md:grid-cols-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">FAMILY MEETING QUESTION</p><h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl">One whole job. One clear owner.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Page three has space for each person's name, responsibility and when or what done means.</p></div><div><p class="font-serif text-xl leading-[1.5]">“{prompt}”</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Try it for a week. Review what worked. The goal isn't a perfect system; it's fewer jobs that still depend on one person's reminders.</p></div></div>
<div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2"><div class="border-t-4 border-[#CDDDE1] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">Build the real family chart.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Add adults and kids, assign ownership and print a personalized family chart with the free builder.</p><a href="/family-responsibility-builder" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Free Family Responsibility Builder</a></div><div class="border-t-4 border-[#D4DFC4] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">Start with one child's jobs.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">The Chore Chart Generator gives a child a short, visible list to practice.</p><a href="/chore-chart" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Free Chore Chart Generator</a></div></div>
</div></section>

<section id="problems" class="bg-[#E8D2D6]/20 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">04 · WHEN RESPONSIBILITY DOESN'T STICK</p><h2 class="section-heading">Change the support, not just the volume of your reminders.</h2><p class="section-lede">Missed jobs and arguments are feedback. Find out whether the starting cue, the skill, the expectations or the available time needs adjusting.</p>
<div class="mt-8 space-y-3">{issues.map(([icon,title,detail])=><article class="grid gap-4 border-l-4 border-[#E8D2D6] bg-white p-5 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.3fr]"><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src={art(icon)} width="50" height="50" loading="lazy" alt="" class="size-[50px] shrink-0 object-contain"/><h3 class="font-serif text-xl">{title}</h3></div><p class="text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}</div>
<div class="mt-8 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">The one-week family check-in</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Ask what worked, what was hard and what support needs changing. Don't restart the whole chart every time someone misses a job. The job can stay theirs while the plan improves.</p><div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 text-sm font-semibold"><a href="/resources/kids-chores-without-nagging" class="underline underline-offset-4">Kids' chores without nagging</a><a href="/resources/chore-chart-without-rewards" class="underline underline-offset-4">Chores without rewards</a></div></div>
</div></section>

<section id="printable" class="px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">PRINT AND PRACTICE</p><h2 class="section-heading">A practical guide for sharing the thinking, not just the chores.</h2><p class="section-lede">The four-page guide teaches the method and gives your family a starting agreement. The actual reusable family chart belongs in the free Responsibility Builder.</p>
<div class="mt-9 border border-[#ded8d2] bg-white p-7 sm:p-9"><GuidePageGallery images={images} title="The Family Responsibility System"/><div class="mt-8 text-center"><a href={pdf} download="OMC-Family-Responsibility-System.pdf" class="btn-primary">Download the free PDF</a><p class="mt-2 text-xs">Four US Letter pages · Email requested for first download</p></div></div>
<div class="mt-10 bg-[#FBF7F1] p-7"><p class="eyebrow">KEEP PRACTICING AS A FAMILY</p><h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl">More than a chart. A family learning to own the work together.</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-[1.8]">Organized Family Club builds on this idea with personalized printed family resources and practical guidance. Its <em>Our Family, Our Team</em> theme is about handing over a whole responsibility so it doesn't keep coming back to Mom.</p><a href="/club" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Explore Organized Family Club</a></div>
</div></section></div>
<style>
.omc-guide{font-family:Montserrat,Arial,sans-serif}.omc-guide section[id]{scroll-margin-top:110px}
.omc-guide .eyebrow{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase}
.omc-guide .section-heading{max-width:800px;margin-top:14px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(2rem,4.6vw,3.15rem);line-height:1.16;letter-spacing:-.025em}
.omc-guide .section-lede{max-width:700px;margin-top:16px;font-size:1.06rem;line-height:1.8}
.omc-guide .guide-anchor{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:48px;padding:10px 13px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d8d1cb;border-radius:3px;color:#545454;font-size:14px;font-weight:650;line-height:1.25;text-align:center;text-decoration:none}
.omc-guide .guide-anchor:hover{background:#CDDDE1}.omc-guide .guide-anchor:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #545454;outline-offset:2px}
@media(min-width:640px){.omc-guide .guide-anchor{min-height:44px;padding:9px 14px;font-size:13px}}
</style>
</PublicLayout>
